2
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:05,700
This latest paper from Anthropic explains why Claude misbehaves and it might just be because of us.

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:11,760
So last year in scenarios where Claude 4 was about to be shut down, it would blackmail users to save itself.

4
00:00:12,580 --> 00:00:15,800
This happened not just once or twice, but 96% of the times.

5
00:00:16,770 --> 00:00:21,250
Fast forward to now that number has dropped to zero. But how did Anthropic fix it?

6
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:25,370
Well, they first traced where the behavior even came from.

7
00:00:25,370 --> 00:00:34,710
Turns out, decades of sci-fi novels and rogue AI articles on the internet have trained Claude on the idea that AI is evil and self-preserving by default.
